The Great Pyramid of Giza is the only one of the seven wonders that currently exists.
Raised by the Egyptians in the third century BC, the Great Pyramid is one of the many large pyramid structures constructed to honor the deceased pharaoh.
In the Egyptian Valley of the Dead, on the Giza Plateau, or Giza Necropolis, there are several pyramids (of which the Great Pyramid is the largest), several small tombs, several temples and the great Sphinx.
The Great Pyramid is in honor of Pharaoh Kufu, and many of the smaller pyramids, tombs and temples - in honor of the women and members of his family.
