Krueger National Park (KNP) is located in the north-eastern South Africa and stretches east along the border with Mozambique, to the north is Zimbabwe, and the Crocodile River is its southern border.
The park stretches for 19 500 km2, divided into 14 separate ecozones, in each of which there is different wildlife.
It represents one of South Africa's main attractions and is considered to be the presenter of South Africa's National Parks (SANParks).
Typically, all South African national parks require daily fees for entrance and conservation of the park.
