The stirrups are hanging on both sides of the saddle supports for the rider's legs.
They provide greater stability for the rider, but safety concerns may arise due to the possibility that the rider's legs will get stuck in them.
In the event that a rider is thrown from a horse and his foot gets stuck in the aspiration, he will be dragged if the horse escapes. To minimize this risk, a number of safety measures can be taken.
